  "body": "## What changed\n\nRetry a machining mesh once at half the planning chord when its measured deviation exceeds the requested tolerance.\nKeep the existing minimum chord and all acceptance checks.\nRecord the finer chord in the mesh report.\nThe Solidcraft sample now meshes at the requested 0.005 mm tolerance.\nIts measured deviation is 0.00323090453 mm, with all 53 faces and no open sides.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe display planner measures normal distance at triangle midpoints and centroids.\nThe verifier uses denser samples and conservative parametric distance on rational-spline faces.\nNine sample faces exceeded the verifier's limit at the original planning chord.\nFace 50 measured 0.00684674657 mm against the 0.005 mm limit.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `solidcraft_sample_meshes_within_the_app_chord` failed before the fix and passed after it.\n- Restoring `upstream/main`'s production file made that pin fail again. Restoring the fix made it pass.\n- `solidcraft_sample_still_refuses_an_out_of_tolerance_mesh` passed. At 0.1 mm, face 36 still exceeds tolerance after the retry.\n- `a_bad_tolerance_or_a_spent_time_bound_is_refused_by_name` passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed: one library test and seven machining-mesh tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- Targeted rustfmt and `git diff --check` passed.\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` reported existing differences in unrelated files. No unrelated files were changed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The `.nc` and `.cl` diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe full heavy release bench, UI and end-to-end posting were not run.\nThe sampled deviation check does not prove the continuous closest-surface distance.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone found in the changed files.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: Retry a refused machining mesh once at a finer chord while preserving its requested tolerance and safety checks.\n\nFixes #1463\n",
